body: `
<h2>Nobel Prizes 2026: Science Categories — Poori Revision</h2><p>Nobel Prizes 2026 ki ghoshna <b>5 se 12 October 2026</b> ke beech hui. Is saal ka puraskar rashi <b>12 million Swedish kronor</b> (lagbhag 1.2 million USD) prati puraskar hai. Puraskar samaroh <b>10 December</b> ko hota hai — Stockholm me (Peace ka Oslo me).</p><h3>1. Physiology ya Medicine — 5 October 2026</h3><p><b>Vijeta:</b> <b>Karl Deisseroth</b> (USA, Stanford University), <b>Peter Hegemann</b> (Germany, Humboldt University Berlin) aur <b>Georg Nagel</b> (Germany, University of Würzburg).</p><p><b>Uplabdhि:</b> 'for their discoveries concerning <b>light-gated ion channels and optogenetics</b>'.</p><ul><li><b>Channelrhodopsin</b> — ek prakash-samvedansheel (light-sensitive) protein jo ek-koशikीय shaival (algae) me paya gaya.</li><li>Hegemann aur Nagel ne is protein ki khoj ki; Deisseroth ne ise <b>nerve cells ke liye light-controlled switch</b> me badla.</li><li><b>Optogenetics</b> — prakash se jeevit mastishk ke individual nerve cells ki gatividhi ko <b>on ya off</b> karne ki takneek. Mastishk ke neural circuits ko map karne me kranti.</li><li>Mains angle: Parkinson's, epilepsy aur yaad-dasht (memory) sambandhi bimariyon ke ilaj me bhavishya ki sambhavnayen.</li></ul><h3>2. Physics — 6 October 2026</h3><p><b>Vijeta:</b> <b>Francis Halzen</b> (University of Wisconsin–Madison, USA; mool roop se Belgium).</p><p><b>Uplabdhि:</b> 'for decisive contributions to the <b>IceCube Neutrino Observatory</b> and the discovery of <b>high-energy neutrinos of astrophysical origin</b>'.</p><ul><li><b>IceCube</b> — Antarctica ke <b>Amundsen–Scott South Pole Station</b> par sthit duniya ka sabse bada neutrino detector, <b>2010 se operational</b>.</li><li>Neutrino atyant halki, lagbhag dravyaman-rahit (nearly massless) kanikayen hain jo padarth se lagbhag takraye bina guzar jati hain — inhe pakadna atyant kathin.</li><li>High-energy astrophysical neutrinos se brahmand ke <b>atyant charam (extreme) vatavaran</b> — jaise black holes aur supernovae — ka adhyayan sambhav hua.</li></ul><h3>3. Chemistry — 7 October 2026</h3><p><b>Vijeta:</b> <b>Henri B. Kagan</b> (France, Université Paris-Sud) aur <b>Kenso Soai</b> (Japan, Tokyo University of Science).</p><p><b>Uplabdhि:</b> 'for the discovery of <b>non-linear effects and autocatalysis in asymmetric organic synthesis</b>'.</p><ul><li><b>Asymmetric synthesis</b> — aisi rasayanik abhikriyayen jo do darpan-pratibimb (mirror-image) roopon me se <b>ek ko visheshataya</b> banati hain. Ise <b>chirality</b> kehte hain.</li><li>Kagan ne <b>non-linear effects</b> khoje; Soai ne <b>asymmetric autocatalysis</b> (Soai reaction) khoji — ek chhota asantulan bhi badi matra me ek roop ko badha sakta hai.</li><li><b>Mains/Prelims angle:</b> dawaon (medicines) ke design me atyant mahatvapurna — do mirror forms me se ek upyogi aur doosra hanikarak ho sakta hai (thalidomide udaharan).</li></ul><blockquote><b>Prelims Rapid Facts:</b> Nobel ki sthapna Alfred Nobel ki vasiyat (1895) se; pehla puraskar 1901; mool 5 shreniyan; Economic Sciences 1968 me Sweden ke central bank (Riksbank) dwara. 2026 me Literature — Anne Carson (Canada), Peace — Navanethem 'Navi' Pillay, Economics — Robert E. Hall aur Michael Woodford.</blockquote>
`
